# The written cell wall: success scene for the writing spot.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_MonCellWall

== start ==
The chalk lines cover the wall, packed close. It is the same evening prayer, written once a night for years. And over the years, the words change.

KEEP US QUIET, LORD becomes KEEP IT QUIET. HOLD US IN YOUR HAND becomes just HOLD.

* [Follow it down the wall.] -> down

== down ==
Near the floor the prayer is gone entirely. One word, once a night: whole. whole. whole.

The last line was written by somebody lying down: LET ME BE WHOLE.

That is not a monk's prayer. That is the crown's wanting, coming out through a dying man's hand.

* [Step out of the cell.] -> end
